## Outcome
`src/main/browser/browserHost.ts` exports `createBrowserHost(deps)`. Per chat, the host:
- owns one agent tab and at most one sign-in tab;
- places the visible one over the rail's Browser area;
- tracks state;
- holds the chat's pending origin prompt.

## Design
- **Deps** (injected, so tests need no Electron):
  - `createView(webPreferences & {partition})` → `{webContents, setBounds, setVisible}`;
  - `attach(view)` / `detach(view)` on the main window's `contentView` (electron.d.ts:3643, :15892, :15906);
  - `zoomFactor()` of the main window's renderer (:18106);
  - `policy` (`s3-origin`), `sites` (the site store), `harden` (`s3-browsersession`), `ownership` (`s3-ownership`), and `push(BrowserState)`.
- **Tabs:** `ensureAgentTab(ref)` creates the view lazily, in the folder's partition. `openSignIn(ref, url)` and `closeSignIn(ref)` use an in-memory partition, and the sign-in tab is never returned to agent APIs.
- **Navigation:** `navigate(ref, url, by: 'agent'|'person')` runs `normalizeTarget` and `decideNavigation` **before** `webContents.loadURL`, because main-initiated loads fire no `will-navigate` (spike item 4).
  - `ask` creates the chat's `pendingOrigin {id, origin, url, requestedBy}`, pushes state and returns `{code:'origin_blocked'}`. There is one pending origin per chat: a newer ask replaces an older unanswered one, which resolves as denied.
  - A person navigating to a new origin is asked too: the card is the consent.
- **Decisions:** `decideOrigin(ref, promptId, 'once'|'always'|'deny')`:
  - once → add the origin to the tab's once set and load the URL;
  - always → `sites.add`, then load;
  - deny → clear the prompt;
  - a stale id → `{code:'stale_prompt'}`.
- **View placement:** `setView(ref, boundsCss|null)` multiplies the bounds by the zoom factor to get DIP, then calls `setBounds` (:15940) and `setVisible(true)` (:15941). Every other chat's view gets `setVisible(false)`, and null hides the view. Views are attached once and removed on dispose.
- **State:** `did-start-loading`, `did-stop-loading`, `did-navigate`, `page-title-updated` and `render-process-gone` update `{url, title, loading}` and push `BrowserState`, including ownership and `ownerLabel`. URLs and titles pushed to the renderer are masked.
- **Lifecycle:**
  - `disposeChat(ref)` destroys the chat's views; call it from chat deletion beside `chatImages.deleteChat`.
  - `dispose()` closes everything; it is added to quit disposal by `s3-browserdispatch`.

## Tests
New `src/main/browser/browserHost.test.ts`, with fake views:
- lazy creation in the folder's partition;
- an agent navigating to an unlisted origin gets origin_blocked, raises one pending prompt, and loadURL is never called;
- the once, always and deny decisions (always persists to the site store);
- a newer ask supersedes an older one;
- a stale decision is refused;
- setView converts with zoom 1.25 and hides other chats' views;
- the sign-in tab uses an in-memory partition and is excluded from `agentTab(ref)`;
- disposeChat and dispose destroy views;
- pushed URLs mask a planted `dmg_` token.

## Final red-team fixes (binding; where a fix contradicts text above, the fix wins)

**Fix 50 [major]** A page can raise origin prompts itself, through script navigations, meta refresh, redirects or iframes, because the session's 'ask' path calls onAsk from page events. The host keeps one pending prompt per chat, a newer ask supersedes and denies the older one, and the card says '<requester> wants to open'. A hostile page on an allowed origin can therefore wipe out the agent's real prompt and show a card for an origin it chose, labelled as the agent's request. Allow once then loads that URL. Ordinary iframes (ads, embeds) also spam cards.

**Required change:** Add to s3-browserhost: "Asks that come from page events have `requestedBy:'page'` (extend the enum in s3-browsercontract), and the card reads 'This page wants to open <origin>'. A page ask never supersedes an agent or person prompt; it is dropped and logged while one is pending. Page asks are limited to one per tab per 10 s. Subframe navigations (`will-frame-navigate` with `isMainFrame:false`) to an unlisted origin are denied silently and never ask." Tests: "a page ask does not replace an agent prompt; a second page ask within 10 s is dropped; an iframe to an unlisted origin is denied with no prompt".

**Fix 52 [major]** Several pairs of tickets edit the same file with no ordering between them (no requires path either way). s3-browserhost also refers to wiring that none of its prerequisites produces.

**Required change:** Add requires: s3-browserdispatch requires += ['s3-imgsend']; s3-origincard requires += ['s3-imgthumbs']; s3-e2eimg requires += ['s3-browsercmds']. Remove the deletion wiring from s3-browserhost (keep `disposeChat` itself) and add to s3-browserdispatch: "wire `host.disposeChat(ref)` into the chat delete path in `src/main/agents/chatStore.ts`, next to the `chatImages.deleteChat` call that s3-imgstore added".

