## Outcome
`src/main/browser/browserDriver.ts` exports `createBrowserDriver(contents, {signal})`. It implements the agent ops on one tab through `webContents.debugger` (electron.d.ts:18570; `attach` :7596, `detach` :7600, `sendCommand` :7612, the `detach` event :7490), using only the commands `docs/reports/agent-browser.md` recorded as GO.

## Ops
- **`attach()`** once per agent session (`'1.3'`); **`detach()`** is idempotent. The `detach` event marks the driver detached, so the next op re-attaches, unless ownership says stopped or person.
- **`read({mode, maxChars})`:** `Accessibility.getFullAXTree` → one line per meaningful node, `[e<n>] <role> "<name>"`. Text mode keeps only names and static text.
  - Refs `e1…` map to `backendDOMNodeId`. They reset on every navigation, and an old ref gets `stale_ref`.
  - Password fields show as `[e<n>] textbox (password)`, with no value.
  - Clip to `maxChars`, set `truncated`, and wrap the result as `{untrusted: true, …}`.
- **`click(ref)`:** `DOM.scrollIntoViewIfNeeded` and `DOM.getBoxModel({backendNodeId})` → the centre of the content quad → `Input.dispatchMouseEvent` pressed, then released (left button, clickCount 1).
- **`type(ref, text, submit)`:**
  - refuse with `secret_refused` when the text matches a secret pattern;
  - refuse with `password_field` when the target is a password field (the person signs in through Take control);
  - otherwise `DOM.focus` plus `Input.insertText`, then Enter when `submit` is set.
- **`press(key)`:** a fixed table → `Input.dispatchKeyEvent` keyDown and keyUp, with `key`, `code` and `windowsVirtualKeyCode`.
- **`screenshot()`:** `contents.capturePage()` (:17922) → a PNG `Buffer`. An empty image → `navigation_failed`.
- **Abort and deadlines:** every op checks the ownership `signal` before and after each `sendCommand`. An aborted signal rejects with `stopped`, and no further commands are sent. Each op has a 20 s deadline (`navigation_failed` or `timeout`) and is never retried.

## Tests
New `src/main/browser/browserDriver.test.ts`, with a fake debugger that records `sendCommand` and replays a golden AX tree, `src/main/browser/__fixtures__/axTree.json` (built from the spike's fixture page):
- the read output and the ref mapping;
- no password value appears;
- maxChars truncation;
- click sends the two mouse events at the quad centre;
- type refuses a `dmg_` text and a password field, and otherwise inserts the text;
- the press table for Enter and Tab;
- a stale ref after a simulated navigation;
- an abort mid-op stops further commands;
- a detach event leads to re-attach on the next op.

